#
# Counter-example for math:FittedModelShape: a fitted model that names its specification
# (math:modelFormula) but is NOT bound to any data — a fitted model is a statistical model
# bound to concrete data, so a model with no math:fittedToData is ill-formed. It fails ONLY
# on sh:minCount 1 for math:fittedToData, so validation MUST emit
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:UnfittedModel).
# Bound by ex:ecFittedModelUnfitted.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:fit a math:FittedModel ;
    math:modelFormula ex:formula .
ex:formula a math:ModelFormula ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:slot0 .
ex:slot0 a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 0 ; math:slotExpression ex:respVar .
ex:respVar a math:VariableExpression .
